// @trap
// @hint redundant type annotation: `k` is inferred as `i32` — remove it to lean on inference
// `u as! i32` over a type parameter pinned at no number is never the target, so it traps, the
// `as!` twin of `as?` answering `null` there, not a boolean read as its bit (D2791).
function k<T>(u: T): i32 { u as! i32 }
print(k(true))
print(-1)
